(I)--a Vindhya clan;
1: Br. II. १६. ६४; वा. ४५. १३२; ८६. २८.
in द्वारवती: one of the five clans (गणस्) of the Haihayas beginning with Druhyu, son of ययाति;
2: Br. III. ६९. ५२; ७४. २६५; M. ३४. ३०; ४३. ४८; ४४. ६९; १६३. ७२; वा. ९४. ५२.
had two hundred branches;
3: Ib. ९९. ४५२.
all of them क्षत्रियस्;
4: Ib. ३२. ४८.
कश्यप gotraka1ras.
5: M. १९९. 2.

(II)--a यादव tribe to which Kamsa belonged: were related to the पाण्डवस्;
1: भा. X. 1. ३५, ३७ and ६९; IX. २४. ११ and ६३; I. १४. २५; M. ११४. ५२; २७३. ७०.
defended द्वारका against the enemies and praised the heroic deeds of कृष्ण;
2: भा. I. ११. ११; IX. २४. ६३.
Kamsa planned in vain to vanquish them. Fought with their kith and kin and ended their lives;
3: Ib. X. ३६. ३३; ३९. २५; XI. ३०. १८.
line of the, traced from महा- bhoja; kings of मृत्तिकावर Pura; hence मार्त्तिकावरस्: killed सात्वत S4atrughna and left द्वारका with अक्रूर.
4: Vi. IV. १३. 7, ११.
